course: dictionary
lesson: 1740
title: Clanging: sound and meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clanging describes a loud, ringing noise made when metal hits metal, like a bell, a pan or a gate. Say the word out loud and you can almost hear it.
explain: Writers also use clanging to describe the way something sounds. Paul wrote that without love a person is only «a clanging cymbal», however great their gifts and knowledge. A cymbal makes a loud, crashing noise, but noise alone is not music, so Paul means that gifts without love make only empty noise.
explain: Clanger is also an informal word. To «drop a clanger» means to make a big, embarrassing mistake. When you read it in a story, look at the words around it to see whether the writer means a real noise or a silly slip.
fact: Clanging means making a loud, ringing sound, like metal hitting metal.
fact: A clanging sound is loud, harsh and ringing.
fact: In «a clanging cymbal», the word shows a loud noise with no real meaning behind it.
fact: The informal phrase «drop a clanger» means to make a big, embarrassing mistake.
fact: Clang, clangs, clanged and clanging are all forms of the same verb.
exercise: Paul writes that without love a person is only «a clanging cymbal». What does clanging describe here? | Bright and shiny | Quiet and calm | Soft and gentle | *Loud, harsh and ringing
exercise: The old gate went clanging shut behind us. Which thing makes a clanging sound? | A whispered song | A soft pillow | *A metal pan dropped on the floor | A feather falling slowly
exercise: Dad says, «You dropped a clanger, Sam!» What does he mean? | Sam dropped a metal pan | Sam won a prize | *Sam made a big, embarrassing mistake | Sam lost his bag
test: The clanging of the pots filled the kitchen. What does clanging describe here? | A soft humming | A smell of cooking | A quiet knock | *A loud ringing of metal
test: Which phrase is an informal idiom meaning a big, embarrassing mistake? | Make a sound | *Drop a clanger | Ring a bell | Clang shut
exam: Paul says that without love a person is «a clanging cymbal». What is he saying? | Love makes loud noises | Clanging is always good | Cymbals are the best instruments | *Gifts without love are just empty noise
